    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d321">

                <pb facs="0658" n="548" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg548"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr. Porter.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-07-29"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 29,
                        1890</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 72.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 101 of the 9th instant, reporting that you had brought the case of Nicolino
                    Mileo to the attention of the Italian Government, which had promised a prompt
                    and thorough investigation of it.</p>
                <p>Awaiting your further reply upon this subject, and adding that the claimant’s
                    attorney has been advised of the presentation of the case and of the promise of
                    the Italian Government respecting it,</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
